<section class="wrap narrow pad prose">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 14 November 2026</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Account details:</b> name, email, optional mobile number, and a securely hashed password (we never store your password itself).</li>
    <li><b>Profile details you choose to give:</b> state, district, PIN code, age or date of birth, and optional information such as income range, education, occupation, family circumstances, social category and disability information.</li>
    <li><b>Saved schemes and preferences</b>, and basic security logs (sign-ins, changes to your account).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do <b>not</b> ask for or store Aadhaar numbers, bank account details, OTPs or passwords for any other service. Please never share these with anyone claiming to represent HaqSetu.</p>
  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <p>Only to show you schemes you may be eligible for, to let you track them, and to keep your account secure. We do not sell your data or use it for advertising. Sensitive details (such as disability or social category) are optional and used only for matching.</p>
  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Edit your profile at any time, or turn off profile-based matching in <a href="/account">Account & privacy</a>.</li>
    <li>Download all your data as a file from <a href="/account">Account & privacy</a>.</li>
    <li>Delete your account permanently; your profile and saved schemes are removed immediately.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We aim to handle personal data in line with India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023. For questions or grievances, contact the site operator using the details published on this site.</p>
  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>Passwords are hashed with bcrypt, sessions are stored server-side with secure cookies, all traffic is encrypted (HTTPS), and sign-in attempts are rate-limited.</p>
  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use one essential session cookie to keep you signed in and to protect forms. We use no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
</section>
